From: Scrumpper <190908034+Scrumpper@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 22:37:33 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 30/59] arm64: dts: rockchip: h96-max-v58: drop Android vendor
 storage, disable OP-TEE

rk3588-android.dtsi adds vendor-storage (rockchip,ram-vendor-storage)
and its size-0 reserved-memory placeholder vendor-storage-rm, filled in
by Android loaders only. No driver is built (ROCKCHIP_RAM_VENDOR_STORAGE
unset) and 6.12 logs "failed to reserve memory for node
'vendor-storage-rm@00000000'". The booted 6.1 DTB has neither node.
drm-logo and drm-cubic-lut stay: U-Boot fills them when it hands over a
logo or LUT, and display-subsystem references drm_logo.

The loader FIT carries no BL32, so the optee node fails the same way on
6.1 and 6.12 ("api uid mismatch", probe error -22). Disable it; a
loader with OP-TEE can re-enable it. 6.12 t6.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01P6itje71iKPFBX7YKkfvRo
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-h96-max-v58.dts | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-h96-max-v58.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-h96-max-v58.dts
index 8a43422c8..e1a9b40e2 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-h96-max-v58.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-h96-max-v58.dts
@@ -71,6 +71,15 @@ wireless_wlan: wireless-wlan {
 	};
 };
 
+/* Android RAM vendor storage: no driver in this kernel */
+/delete-node/ &vendor_storage;
+/delete-node/ &vendor_storage_rm;
+
+/* no BL32 in the loader */
+&optee {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
+
 /* GPU: Panthor binding on the vendor node, so the device stays fb000000.gpu */
 &gpu {
 	compatible = "rockchip,rk3588-mali", "arm,mali-valhall-csf";
